    <description>DIR-868. After a contract is created from a bundle quote, the standard CreateContract action does not emit ContractItemPrice rows for the installment products (grandchildren under the payment plan). While the contract is still Draft, this flow reads the Unit and Payment Plan CIP rows, finds the selected plan's installment components on ProductRelatedComponent, and creates one Installment CIP row per component with its percentage and computed amount (unit price x percentage). Guarded by Contract.RES_CIP_Installments_Generated__c and Status = Draft. All DML has fault paths so a failure never rolls back the triggering save.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>fInstallmentAmount</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    OR(ISBLANK({!Get_Unit_CIP.Price}), ISBLANK({!Loop_Installment_Components.RES_Installment_Percentage__c})),
    0,
    ({!Get_Unit_CIP.Price} * {!Loop_Installment_Components.RES_Installment_Percentage__c}) / 100
)</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>RES Contract AfterSave Generate Installment CIP {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>RES Contract AfterSave Generate Installment CIP</label>
